# Resources
[(back to project README)](../README.md)

## What's in this directory

Resource YAML files define Databricks resources deployed by the bundle. Files in this
directory are auto-discovered via the `include: ./resources/*.yml` directive in
`databricks.yml`.

After running `uv run setup` with an agent template, this directory will contain:

| File | Resources |
|------|-----------|
| `app-resource.yml` | Databricks App — serves your agent via MLflow AgentServer |

Additional resource files can be added for other components (jobs, model serving
endpoints, etc.). Any `.yml` file placed here is automatically included in the bundle.

## How Databricks Asset Bundles work

Resources are defined as YAML and deployed together with your code via
`databricks bundle deploy`. The CLI reads `databricks.yml` (the bundle root),
resolves variable substitutions for the target environment, and creates or updates
each resource in the workspace.

Key patterns:
- **`${bundle.target}`** — replaced with the target name (dev, staging, prod). Used
  in resource names to avoid collisions across environments.
- **`${var.variable_name}`** — bundle variables defined in `databricks.yml`. Override
  per-target under `targets.<name>.variables`.

## Deployment targets

| Target | When | Mode |
|--------|------|------|
| dev | Manual (`databricks bundle deploy -t dev`) | development |
| staging | Merge to `main` (via CI/CD) | default |
| prod | Merge to `release` (via CI/CD) | production |

## Validate and deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate -t dev
databricks bundle deploy -t dev
```

## Clean up

```bash
databricks bundle destroy -t dev
```

This removes bundle-managed resources. Data assets (tables, volumes, vector search
indexes) not managed by the bundle must be removed manually.

## Adding resources

Add a `.yml` file to this directory following the DAB resource schema. Run
`databricks bundle schema` to see available resource types and properties.

```bash
databricks bundle validate -t dev    # check config after changes
databricks bundle deploy -t dev      # deploy
```

[Databricks Asset Bundles resource reference](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/dev-tools/bundles/resources)

